%% Pull-based deploy: no AWS credentials ever leave AWS.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant GH as GitHub repo + Actions
    participant EC2 as EC2 · poll.sh (systemd timer, every 60 s)
    participant SSM as SSM Parameter Store
    participant App as Docker: app + Caddy
    participant User as Live site /health

    Dev->>GH: git push to main
    GH->>GH: job "test": pytest vs Postgres<br/>job "build": docker build
    loop every 60 seconds
        EC2->>GH: git fetch main: new commit?
        EC2->>GH: Checks API: did "test" pass for it?
    end
    GH-->>EC2: yes, new commit, tests passed
    EC2->>SSM: read DB host/user/password (instance IAM role)
    EC2->>App: docker build + compose up --wait
    App-->>EC2: container /health healthy (DB reachable)
    alt new version never healthy
        EC2->>App: roll back to previous image, mark commit bad
    end
    GH->>User: job "verify-deploy": poll /health
    User-->>GH: version == pushed commit → pipeline green
